      "expected": "The specification says each TMC2209 5VOUT is not tied to the board main +5V rail; it should form a local per-driver reference rail (/5V_pH, /5V_NA, /5V_NB) for the current-reference divider.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U9 ... 5VOUT ... +5V; U1 ... 5VOUT ... +5V; U6 ... 5VOUT ... +5V"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Each TMC2209 ... internal 5V linear regulator output (\"5VOUT\") that is NOT tied to the board's main +5V rail ... i.e. a per-driver reference rail, not a shared supply."}
      ],
      "impact": "The internal 5V regulator outputs are paralleled/back-fed with the buck +5V rail, which can corrupt the motor current reference, cause regulator contention, or damage the drivers.",
      "confidence": 0.66
    },
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["PR4", "H4"],
      "pins": ["PR4.1", "PR4.2", "PR4.3", "H4.1", "H4.2", "H4.3"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0057", "NET0033"],
      "observed": "The WATER LEVEL SENSOR/SWITCHES sheet shows a LiDAR water-height sensor PR4 connected through H4 to +5V and the main I2C nets NET0057/NET0033.",
      "expected": "The specification states the TF-Luna LiDAR is present but not wired, and the wired water-level sensing path is an ultrasonic sensor on GPIOs, not an I2C LiDAR.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Water Height Sensor ... PR4 LiDAR ... NET0057 ... NET0033"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "TF-Luna LiDAR module (PR1) ... its pins are \"free\" ... not wired into any net ... water-level sensing that is actually wired and actually used by firmware is an HC-SR04-style ultrasonic sensor read on two ESP32 GPIOs."}
      ],
      "impact": "The board contains an implemented I2C LiDAR water-level path that the documented firmware does not use, changing the sensor behavior and adding an unexpected I2C device/load.",
      "confidence": 0.52
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains at least two clear deviations from the intended r2 design: the ATO valve MOSFET is AO3400A instead of the specified AON6407, and the TMC2209 5VOUT pins are tied to the global +5V rail rather than kept as local reference rails. A third likely deviation is the LiDAR water-height sensor being wired to I2C despite the specification documenting the LiDAR as unwired."
}

